      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The concept of \"global governance\" is a direct, existential challenge to the Westphalian model of absolute national sovereignty. Any attempt to impose supranational law inherently means ceding decision-making power to unelected international bodies, which is an unacceptable surrender of self-determination. True national sovereignty demands that the ultimate authority rests exclusively with the nation-state, making deep integration into global governance structures a fundamental compromise of national autonomy.",
      "source": "target",
